  "question": {
    "text": "<img width=\"250px\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/EwH99Gb1XY4gu2DxmfucMso6sCYgJk0OryLDi7CFel8.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\n\n\nA piece of granite floats at the interface of mercury and water contained in a beaker as in figure. If the densities of granite, water and mercury are $\\rho, \\rho_1$ and $\\rho_2$ respectively, the ratio of the volume of granite in water to the volume of granite in mercury is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kboQh",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\rho_2-\\rho}{\\rho-\\rho_1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xQopZ",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\rho_2+\\rho}{\\rho_1+\\rho}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "w7aSj",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\rho_1 \\rho_2}{\\rho}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "exYbP",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\rho_1}{\\rho_2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img width=\"250px\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/Yqu92Cu3p3vXNOWng8rOHVo41cPn9C_yZL-ESorPQZg.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & V_1 \\rho_1 g+V_2 \\rho_2 g=V \\rho g \\\\ & \\Rightarrow V_1 \\rho_1 g+V_2 \\rho_2 g=\\left(V_1+V_2\\right) \\rho g \\\\ & \\Rightarrow V_1 \\rho_1 g-V_1 \\rho g=V_2 \\rho g-V_2 \\rho_2 g, \\Rightarrow V_1\\left(\\rho-\\rho_1\\right)=V_2\\left(\\rho_2-\\rho\\right) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\frac{V_1}{V_2}=\\frac{\\rho_{2-} \\rho}{\\rho-\\rho_1}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
